  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV&amp;AIDS project Western Equatoria &#x2013; Development and Peace Office, CDTY</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a 3 year project targeting the church structures at parish level in responding to the fight against HIV&amp;AIDS with the aim of increasing personal and community risk perceptions to reduce and prevent new HIV infections as well as re-infections most especially among the most at risk populations (i.e. youths, teenagers, women, etc) in the 12 parishes in the diocese of Tombura-Yambio. The project targets over 25,000 beneficiaries, majority of who are the most at risk populations, clergy, lay leaders, PLWHAs, diocesan medical staff, and school teachers. The project major components focus on prevention through awareness campaigns, care and support initiatives, advocacy, and capacity building of the diocesan HIV team through development of systems, trainings, and surveys.</narrative>
  </description>
